{
  "title": "CHAPTER 14: IMPORTANT TERMS IN ECONOMICS",
  "order": 13,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "r4ibmzq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. GDP (Gross Domestic Product)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "GDP measures the total value of final goods and services produced domestically, whereas GNP includes net factor income from abroad.",
        "Stagflation is an adverse economic situation where high inflation and high unemployment occur together.",
        "Fiscal deficits reflect total borrowings required, while Primary Deficit isolates fiscal performance by subtracting interest payments.",
        "The RBI controls liquidity using monetary reserve ratios (CRR, SLR) and key lending rates (Repo Rate, Reverse Repo Rate).",
        "Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) grants management control, whereas Foreign Portfolio Investment (FPI) involves financial assets without management control."
      ],
      "id": "gkucpf2"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
